(7591268, 1222025, 138721, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i> So don''t leave me in suspense, what is it?????? This got an 8 from me, as I think it is fantastic! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, this is ferrofluid mixed with colored water ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by JulietNN: So don''t leave me in suspense, what is it?????? This got an 8 from me, as I think it is fantastic!   Yes, this is ferrofluid mixed with colored water ;-)', '2018-08-08 16:38:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7591334, 1222360, 70514, '<td valign="top">Ah, I do like and get what you were going for.  I think this would''ve played better with a tighter crop and macro feel, although, it would take away the "tiny" aspect.  Just love the ideas your eyes have!!!</td>', 'Ah, I do like and get what you were going for.  I think this would''ve played better with a tighter crop and macro feel, although, it would take away the "tiny" aspect.  Just love the ideas your eyes have!!!', '2018-08-08 21:38:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7591347, 1221439, 30490, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Giles:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Catherine_B:</b></div><hr/><i> This image isn''t exactly inspired and the focus of the chairs is very blurry. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Are your eyes ok or maybe your screen is broken? Very blurry!? Or is that because it hasnt been sharpened and sharpened and sharpened again till it starts haloing which seems the dpc way? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well I see blur around the chairs and the arm and the leg. Could be what the photographer intended, but when I give a lower vote I try to tell the photographer why I scored the image lower.  You can appreciate someone giving their honest opinion or not. I personally would rather know why someone gave me a low score than just have people tell me it is great.  I have Facebook and Instagram to stroke my ego, I use DPC to grow and learn and some times that means giving and getting constructive criticism.  I thought that was the point of the site....  oh and for reference mine was not the lowest score given to this image, so maybe that is helpful to the photographer and maybe it isn''t.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-08-08 21:00:59.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Giles: Originally posted by Catherine_B: This image isn''t exactly inspired and the focus of the chairs is very blurry.   Are your eyes ok or maybe your screen is broken? Very blurry!? Or is that because it hasnt been sharpened and sharpened and sharpened again till it starts haloing which seems the dpc way?   Well I see blur around the chairs and the arm and the leg. Could be what the photographer intended, but when I give a lower vote I try to tell the photographer why I scored the image lower.  You can appreciate someone giving their honest opinion or not. I personally would rather know why someone gave me a low score than just have people tell me it is great.  I have Facebook and Instagram to stroke my ego, I use DPC to grow and learn and some times that means giving and getting constructive criticism.  I thought that was the point of the site....  oh and for reference mine was not the lowest score given to this image, so maybe that is helpful to the photographer and maybe it isn''t.', '2018-08-08 21:59:49.000000', '2018-08-08 22:00:59.000000', 0),
(7591459, 1221977, 86090, '<td valign="top">I though this was awesome. I know by experience how difficult is to get a butterfly in motion, and with that much detail. Very impress with your skills.</td>', 'I though this was awesome. I know by experience how difficult is to get a butterfly in motion, and with that much detail. Very impress with your skills.', '2018-08-09 17:14:51.000000', NULL, 0);
